		)
		(uuid "10b1f4a8-307d-5d5f-a363-d49fc459d6b8")
	)
	(text "USB-C receptacle, 24 pins (USB 3 and USB 2.0; power sink, 5 V only, no USB PD)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "23fd3b15-ce12-554f-a3e1-aafe20139fe1")
	)
	(text "SEL low (plug upright, CC1) -> port B = TX1 / RX1; SEL high (flipped, CC2) -> port C = TX2 / RX2.  Port A: the FX3.\nThe FX3's transmitter has its 100 nF coupling capacitors here; its receiver needs none (AN70707 figure 15).\nPins 1 / 10 are NC on the HD3SS3212 and VDD on the PI3USB302-A: tied to VCC.\nThe switch is passive and bidirectional: channel 0 (A0 / B0 / C0) carries the transmit pairs and channel 1 the\nreceive pairs.  This order and the polarity are chosen for the layout: all four SuperSpeed pairs reach the\nreceptacle on the top layer without crossing, and the FX3 transmitter's '+' line reaches the receptacle's '-'\ncontact (likewise on the receive side).  USB 3.2 section 6.4.2 requires every SuperSpeed receiver to detect and\ncorrect lane polarity, the FX3's and the host's alike."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 386.239 44.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "29475591-54b7-5e55-b42a-150a5cad7fe1")
	)
	(text "The host pulls up the CC pin that its cable connects (0.25 ... 2.04 V across our 5.1k); the other CC pin stays at 0 V.\nSS_SEL = CC2 > CC1.  The 100k / 10n filters (1 ms) average out USB PD messages (BMC, 0 ... 1.1 V) that a PD source\nmay send on the active CC pin, so the switch never changes over during a connection.  10M gives 33 mV hysteresis\n(the two filtered CC pins differ by 0.25 V or more once a cable is in).\nTest points on CC1, CC2 and SS_SEL; none on D+ / D- or the SuperSpeed pairs, where a pad would be a stub."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 223.863 37.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b418abeb-bdc7-5a77-bee7-7f27739ac84d")
	)
